  "title": "85: al-Burooj البروج",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالسَّمَآءِ ذَاتِ الْبُرُوْجِۙ‏(1)\nWAS SAMAAA-E ZAATIL BOROOJE.\nBy the heaven with its Houses,\nوَالْيَوْمِ الْمَوْعُوْدِۙ‏(2)\nWAL YAWMIL MAW-O’ODE.\nby the Promised Day,\nوَشَاهِدٍ وَّمَشْهُوْدٍؕ‏(3)\nWA SHAAHEDINW WA MASHHOOD.\nby the Witness and the Witnessed:\nقُتِلَ اَصْحٰبُ الْاُخْدُوْدِۙ‏(4)\nQOTELA ASHAABUL UKHDOODIN.\nperish the People of the Ditch!\nالنَّارِ ذَاتِ الْوَقُوْدِۙ‏(5)\nNAARE ZAATIL WAQOODE.\nThe fire abounding in fuel,\nاِذْ هُمْ عَلَيْهَا قُعُوْدٌ ۙ‏(6)\nIZ HUM A’LAYHAA QO-O’ODUNW.\nabove which they sat\nوَّهُمْ عَلٰى مَا يَفْعَلُوْنَ بِالْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ شُهُوْدٌ ؕ‏(7)\nWA HUM A’LAA MAA YAF-A’LOONA BIL-MOA-MENEENA SHO-HOOD.\nas they were themselves witnesses to what they did to the faithful.\nوَمَا نَقَمُوْا مِنْهُمْ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يُّؤْمِنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ الْعَزِيْزِ الْحَمِيْدِۙ‏(8)\nWA MAA NAQAMOO MINHUM ILLAA AN-Y YOA-MENOO BIL-LAAHIL A’ZEEZIL HAMEEDIL.\nThey were vindictive towards them only because they had faith in Allah, the All-mighty and the All-laudable,\nالَّذِىْ لَهٗ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ؕ وَ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ شَهِيْدٌ ؕ‏(9)\nLAZEE LAHOO MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL-ARZ, WAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN SHAHEED.\nto whom belongs the kingdom of the heavens and the earth, and Allah is witness to all things.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ فَتَنُوا الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَ الْمُؤْمِنٰتِ ثُمَّ لَمْ يَتُوْبُوْا فَلَهُمْ عَذَابُ جَهَنَّمَ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابُ الْحَرِيْقِؕ‏(10)\nINNAL LAZEENA FATANUL MOA-MENEENA WAL MOAMENAATE SUMMA LAM YATOOBOO FALAHUM A’ZAABO JAHANNAMA WA LAHUM A’ZAABUL HAREEQ.\nIndeed those who persecute the faithful, men and women, and do not repent thereafter, there is the punishment of hell for them and the punishment of burning.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ لَهُمْ جَنّٰتٌ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ ؕؔ ذٰلِكَ الْفَوْزُ الْكَبِيْرُؕ‏(11)\nINNAL LAAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE LAHUM JANNAATUN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAAR, ZAALEKAL FAWZUL KABEER.\nIndeed those who have faith and do righteous deeds—for them will be gardens with streams running in them. That is the supreme success.\nاِنَّ بَطْشَ رَبِّكَ لَشَدِيْدٌ ؕ‏(12)\nINNA BATSHA RABBEKA LA-SHADEED.\nIndeed your Lord’s striking is severe.\nاِنَّهٗ هُوَ يُبْدِئُ وَيُعِيْدُ‌ ۚ‏(13)\nINNAHU HOWA YUBDEO WA YO-E’ED.\nIt is indeed He who originates and brings back,\nوَهُوَ الْغَفُوْرُ الْوَدُوْدُۙ‏(14)\nWA HOWAL GHAFOORUL WADOODO.\nand He is the All-forgiving, the All-affectionate,\nذُو الْعَرْشِ الْمَجِيْدُ ۙ‏(15)\nZUL A’RSHIL MAJEEDO.\nLord of the Throne, the All-glorious,\nفَعَّالٌ لِّمَا يُرِيْدُ ؕ‏(16)\nFA’-A’ALUL LEMAA YOREED.\ndoer of what He desires.\nهَلْ اَتٰٮكَ حَدِيْثُ الْجُنُوْدِۙ‏(17)\nHAL ATAAKA HADEESUL JONOODE.\nDid you receive the story of the hosts\nفِرْعَوْنَ وَثَمُوْدَؕ‏(18)\nFIR-A’WNA WA SAMOOD.\nof Pharaoh and Thamud?\nبَلِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا فِىْ تَكْذِيْبٍۙ‏(19)\nBALIL LAZEENA KAFAROO FEE TAKZEEBINW.\nIndeed the faithless dwell in denial,\nوَّاللّٰهُ مِنْ وَّرَآئِهِمْ مُّحِيْطٌۚ‏(20)\nWAL LAAHO MINW WA-RAAA-EHIM MOHEET.\nand Allah besieges them from all around.\nبَلْ هُوَ قُرْاٰنٌ مَّجِيْدٌ ۙ‏(21)\nBAL HOWA QURAANUM MAJEEDUN.\nIndeed it is a glorious Quran,\nفِىْ لَوْحٍ مَّحْفُوْظٍ‏(22)\nFEE LAWHIM MAHFOOZ.\nin a preserved tablet.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Burooj (The Mansion Of Stars)\nThis ‘Makki’ Surah has 22 verses. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the one who recites this Surah will be near the Prophets and Messengers on the Day of Judgement. The reward for reciting this Surah is ten times the number of people who gather on the plains of Arafah.\nReciting this Surah saves one from dangers and if recited before sleeping, one is kept under the protection of Allah (s.w.t.) for the whole night. When trying to wean a baby (stop it from breastfeeding and start eating solid foods), this Surah should be written and tied as a talisman around the baby’s neck."
